title: Authorizations › Worklist › Arrive and read the views
route: /authorizations
intro: Authorizations is one workspace for every authorization, from preparation to the payer's decision and the approved authorization's reviews. The page is a title, the payer signal, one row of view chips with counts, the filter bar and one table. Every part has its own diagram; this one shows the ways in and how the page is laid out.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: the counts are the seed data for Both sites (95 rows: 19 in progress, 36 with the payer, 32 approved, 8 denied; 30 need attention; 47 reviews due this week). There is no subtitle and there are no figure tiles: the view chips carry the counts. Case Manager is no longer a page; its functions are views and rows of this list.
---
start s1 "Click 'Authorizations' or 'All Authorizations' in the sidebar"
start s2 "Demo menu › Suggested path › 'Authorizations: every request in one list' (step 2)\nor 'Authorizations: reviews this week' (step 7, opens ?view=reviews)"
start s3 "On a case page or the ledger case page: click 'Back to Authorizations' or the 'Authorizations' crumb"
start s4 "An old Case Manager address (/manager, /active) or a link from another tab"
goto gOld "Continues in: Authorizations › Old links › Case Manager addresses and links from other tabs"

decision dA "Is the address plain /authorizations, and was a view or a filter used since the page was loaded?"
process pR "The last view and filters come back\nA reload forgets them; ?quick= and ?review= are never brought back"
process pN "The address decides the view and the filters\nNone named: All, no filter"
screen pg "Authorizations\nTitle, payer signal, view chips, filter bar, one table"
process sb "Sidebar: 'All Authorizations' turns green under 'Authorizations'\nThe 'Authorizations' badge reads 19: open requests due now or within 24 hours"

screen hd "Title 'Authorizations', with a small 'Site A' tag when one site is in view\nButton 'New Case' on the right, no subtitle"
process hb "Buttons before 'New Case' follow the view\nReviews this week: 'Draft all due reviews' and 'Sign all clean drafts'\nWith the payer: '4 sent today', only when something was sent today"
click cN "Click 'New Case'"
goto gN "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › How a case starts and resumes"
click cS "Click '4 sent today'"
process pS "Go to /dashboard?stage=received"
goto gS "Continues in: Dashboard › Lifecycle › Click a state to filter the table"
goto gR "Continues in: Authorizations › Reviews this week › Draft all due reviews and sign all clean drafts"

screen bn "One-line payer signal banner\nOnly while a request at the sites in view is affected and it was not dismissed"
goto gB "Continues in: Authorizations › Worklist › Cardinal payer signal"
screen ch "View chips with counts, in three groups\n'All 95' and 'Needs attention 30'\n'In progress 19', 'With the payer 36', 'Approved 32', 'Denied 8'\n'Reviews this week 47'"
goto gV "Continues in: Authorizations › Worklist › Pick a view"
screen fb "Filter bar\nSearch, 'All payers', 'All services', 'All request types', 'Any deadline', 'More'"
goto gF "Continues in: Authorizations › Worklist › Search and filter"

screen tb "Table card\n'95 authorizations' on the left\n'Approval chance, open requests 79%' and an info icon on the right"
process av "The average is worked out from the In progress and With the payer rows that pass the filters"
click ci "Hover or focus the info icon 'About units and approval chance'"
overlay oi "Tip: units or days left are worked out at the usual pace; 'Runs out before review' appears only when that pace uses the approval up first\nApproval chance: Strong 80 and above, Moderate 55 to 79, At risk below 55. It never blocks a request\nEsc closes it"
screen tr "One row per authorization, 15 a page\nPatient / request, Status, Next action, Deadline, Owner, Chance and the row's own button"
goto gT "Continues in: Authorizations › Worklist › Read a row"
goto gW "Continues in: Authorizations › Worklist › What makes a row"

s1 --> dA
s2 --> dA
s3 --> dA
s4 --> gOld
dA -->|Yes| pR --> pg
dA -->|No| pN --> pg
pg --> sb
pg --> hd --> hb
hd --> cN --> gN
hb --> cS --> pS --> gS
hb -.-> gR
pg --> bn --> gB
pg --> ch --> gV
pg --> fb --> gF
pg --> tb --> av
tb --> ci --> oi
tb --> tr --> gT
tr -.-> gW
